# Finite internal scheduling of consumed-memory preparation, with the local program interface open

Status: provisional, source-exposed conditional composition. A finite internal clock can replace the control waveform at the level of a completely specified static Hamiltonian and a full retained-output estimate. The construction below has positive ordinary-neighbour clock bonds, but generally three-body, long-range clock–data program terms. It does **not** solve their ordinary-nearest-neighbour two-qubit realization. That missing interface is isolated explicitly in section9. The supplied pure program-clock preparation is also a substantial new resource; this is not autonomous cooling from mixed memory alone.

## 1. Exact premises, domains and overlap

The mathematical sources are the accepted finite-reservoir argument26220ec995a93bd6af725a6b3463d0b676b9d8a864b4867459bef7dd9560e9b4, the provisional biased-memory argumentf38d4590d700db0ce12c491c4e2c21a7843207d226b74089b537519acbd5a86a, and the accepted arbitrary-background unary-cycle argumentc7a19c3acb7d731a95b97bfadc8a32e2624196d60555ac08e8e77b3ad71d1135. All are copied completely. Conditional acceptance records for the first and third are copied; this task does not promote the second or supply an audit verdict. The relevant inherited estimates are restated with their hypotheses below, and the changed serialization/composition is proved here.

The current canonical unary-cycle notefa7028e0 contains that complete33019-byte body exactly once. The current window notebcefbb19 contains the complete b3b6 boundary body at bytes[62134,80595). It supplies the literal installed apparatus through the finite-reservoir parent. Its two other windows are overlap context, not additional mathematical premises. The current static-reader note6f854791 contains revisedfdb9 at[11852,40578). That theorem replaces the added apparatus and records a historical old Pauli using a supplied pure pointer; it does not implement this memory word or attach a controller to the unchanged boundary apparatus. Its conclusions are not imported. Source identity is checked by complete unique extraction, not branch ancestry.

Let D be the finite original occupied chain q_l=(l,0,0),0<=l<n_old,n_old>=2, with its unchanged finite Hermitian onsite/ordinary-NN generator K, including its scalar and any already installed reserve. Let C consist of the original boundary apparatus: L_b+1 heads and eight mediators, L_b>=8, n=L_b+9. Every original C input sector and arbitrary D-C-R correlations are allowed, where R is passive. The whole operator remains

    H0=K+H_app,    ||K-aI||<=h,
    H_app |vac_C>=0,    0<=H_app<=B I,
    B=||H_app||,    beta=h+B.                              (1)

These are full-qubit-space statements. In the literal parent B=A_head+8 Lambda, with the original coefficients and positive lift unchanged. The center a is an estimate, not an altered physical scalar. H_app need not commute with K. The boundary also has [H0,N_C]=0, but the preparation below need not preserve N_C. No nominal C-sector projection is made in its comparison.

The fresh memory A=E F has zero stipulated free Hamiltonian, and unlisted couplings are absent or charged as faults. E has n qubits, each on the parent's specified neighbouring vacancy e(u),u in C. F contains additional compression trash. Supply

    rho_initial = sigma_DCR tensor Theta_AS,
    Tr_S Theta_AS = tau_q^(tensor nQ),
    tau_q=diag(1-q,q),   0<q<=q_bar<1/2,   Q=3^r,r>=1.     (2)

S is any passive memory purifier; it need not factor across memory sites. The A marginal must be a product and AS must initially factor from DCR. Same one-site biases with unrestricted correlations are insufficient. Every factor D,C,E,F,R,S is retained. An additional finite clock X will be supplied independently in its specified pure state; X is retained too.

## 2. The finite word and a new serial waveform

The biased-memory source gives an explicit reversible majority circuit on each length-Q ray. The chronological three-bit word CX(a,b),CX(a,c),CCX(b,c;a) puts the majority bit into a and retains reversible trash. Recursing on independent subblocks gives

    q_0=q,  q_(j+1)=3q_j^2-2q_j^3,
    p0=(1-q_r)^n,
    ||rho_AS^c-|vac_E><vac_E| tensor omega_FS||_1
       <=delta_r=2sqrt(1-p0)<=2sqrt(n q_r),                 (3)

where rho_AS^c=U_c Theta_AS U_c*, and omega_FS is the normalized vacuum projection comparison. No actual projection or measurement is performed. The bound follows by purifying and projecting: the pure-vector overlap is sqrt(p0), and partial trace contracts. It includes an arbitrary retained S. The stronger linear diagonal bound without a purifier is not used.

The source's phase-exact five-two-qubit Toffoli decomposition and returned-SWAP routes give

    P=n[(20r/3)Q-(7/2)(Q-1)],
    A_c=sum_(p=1)^P ||F_p||
       =n pi[(20r/3)Q-(13/4)(Q-1)].                       (4)

All F_p are positive Hermitian logarithms on a single ordinary NN memory pair. Their full operators, including identity parts, are

    F_SWAP=(pi/2)(I-SWAP),    F_CX=pi Pi,
    F_CV=(3pi/2)Pi,          F_CVdag=(pi/2)Pi,
    Pi=|1><1|_control tensor (I-X_target)/2.               (5)

Thus exp(-iF_p) is the intended gate exactly. Each two-qubit logarithm is rank one and has normalized Pauli scalar ||F_p||/4. The integer word/route construction, bias recurrence and ray geometry are the explicit provisional import; no new claim of generic purification is made.

We change the scheduled waveform, not the word. Choose finite positive t_c,t_s. On each of the P consecutive compression slots of length d_c=t_c/P use the constant Hamiltonian F_p/d_c. Serialize the n reset pairs next: on each slot of length d_s=t_s/n use F_(s,u)/d_s with F_(s,u)=(pi/2)(I-S_(u,e(u))). These resets commute in the comparator because the pairs are disjoint, but only one is driven at any instant. Set the waveform to zero afterwards. There are

    p=P+n,  t0=t_c+t_s,
    c=max(3pi P/(2t_c), pi n/t_s),
    A=A_c+n pi=integral ||V0(t)||dt,
    I_ctl=A_c/4+n pi/4,                                  (6)

where I_ctl is the exact time-integrated data Pauli scalar. Every pulse is positive, acts on at most one NN pair, and has norm at most c. The zero-extended step function has total operator variation

    B_var<=2c p.                                         (7)

Every jump is charged; finite endpoint values on sets of measure zero do not change its propagator. The discontinuous waveform is a comparator used to specify a static program, not a claim that instantaneous physical switches have been built. The previous smooth sin-squared schedule remains unchanged in its source. The present schedule has a different peak/derivative convention and must not inherit its smooth-slope formulas.

## 3. Complete output and the actual aging during the schedule

All compression gates act on A only, so [H0,V0(t)]=0 throughout compression. Consequently its exact endpoint is exp(-it_c H0) tensor U_c. Set

    sigma^c=exp(-it_c H0) sigma exp(it_c H0).              (8)

During serial reset compare the actual H0+V0 to K+V0. The latter has endpoint exp(-it_s K) product_u S_u, because K acts only on D. Duhamel on the **full** DCE space gives operator error at most B t_s. The product swaps transfer the whole original C factor into E, including its D/R correlations, and put C in vacuum on the comparison-ready E input. This reasoning does not rely on a parallel pulse or a one-excitation C input.

Let T_CE be that tensor relabelling. For s>=0 define

    Omega_aged(s)=|vac_C><vac_C| tensor
       exp[-i(t_s+s)K] T_CE sigma^c T_CE*
       exp[i(t_s+s)K] tensor omega_FS.                    (9)

Tensor ordering is notational. The post-reset target evolves under H0 exactly as under K, since H_app annihilates vacuum for every old vector. The ideal reservoir E and trash F keep the transferred information and correlations. If U0(t) is the chronological propagator of H0+V0, then, for every s in any declared finite interval[0,w],

    ||U0(t0+s) rho_initial U0(t0+s)*-Omega_aged(s)||_1
       <=min(2,delta_r+2B t_s).                           (10)

Proof: use(3) after exact compression, then the full-space Duhamel estimate and the pure-isometry trace inequality for reset; common post-reset H0 evolution contracts the existing error and acts as K on the target. F,S are simply additional references during reset. No output is discarded.

If the requested target instead keeps only free old aging from the original supplied input, put

    Omega_free(s)=|vac_C><vac_C| tensor
       exp[-i(t_c+t_s+s)K] T_CE sigma T_CE*
       exp[i(t_c+t_s+s)K] tensor omega_FS.                (11)

The operator difference exp(-it_c H0)-exp(-it_c K) has norm at most B t_c. Thus(10) becomes delta_r+2B(t_c+t_s). This extra term is real; slow compression cannot silently retain(11). The actual H0-aged version(9) allows slow capped compression, while the free-old version forces a short t_c for this sufficient bound. Neither version changes K or installs a cancellation term.

The channel comparison is uniform over sigma and every R, for the fixed supplied reservoir extension Theta_AS. It is also uniform over allowed extensions S in(2), with their corresponding omega_FS. It is not a diamond statement on arbitrary dirty or initially D-correlated reservoirs.

## 4. Finite internal clock, full-space operator and finite choices

Fix a desired window width w>0 and horizon T=t0+w. Let S_c=4T and omega=2pi/S_c. Extend V0 periodically on the circle, with zero comparator control on[t0,S_c). Choose integers R_f,k>=1 and use the positive Fejer kernel

    F_(R_f)(x)=|sum_(l=0)^R_f exp(il omega x)|^2/[S_c(R_f+1)],
    V_R(x)=integral_circle F_(R_f)(y)V0(x-y)dy.             (12)

Every V_R(x) is positive, because every V0(t) is positive. Its norm is at most c. Grouping by actual data support E gives positive pieces V_(R,E), with sum_E||V_(R,E)(x)||<=c. The inherited formula for every finite Fourier coefficient is

    A_(E,0)=S_c^-1 sum_(p:E_p=E) d_p K_p,
    A_(E,q)=(1-|q|/(R_f+1)) sum_(p:E_p=E)
       [exp(-iq omega a_p)-exp(-iq omega b_p)]K_p/(iq omega S_c),
             0<|q|<=R_f,                                (13)

where K_p=F_p/d_p and the n serial reset logarithms are included. Thus V_R(x)=sum_E sum_q exp(iq omega x) A_(E,q), completely specified by the finite word and durations. The q=0 row is understood separately; A_(-q)=A_q*. Exact coefficients are computable, not necessarily rational.

Let M be a multiple of four, a_c=S_c/M and x_j=j a_c. Install M additional physical clock qubits X. With n_j=|1><1| and sigma^+=|1><0|, define

    b_j=[n_j+n_(j+1)+i(sigma_(j+1)^+sigma_j^-
                           -sigma_j^+sigma_(j+1)^-)]/(2a_c),
    K_X=sum_(j=0)^(M-1)b_j,
    V_X=sum_j n_j tensor V_R(x_j),
    H_aut=H0+K_X+V_X.                                    (14)

Clock indices are cyclic. Each actual two-site b_j is positive with norm1/a_c, as seen from its pair-sector eigenvalues0,0,1/a_c,1/a_c. Every term n_j tensor V_R(x_j) is positive on the full space. Hence K_X+V_X>=0 on all clock and data sectors. This does not make H_aut positive for arbitrary signed K: on X vacuum it is still H0. If H0 is already positive, no new positivity reserve is needed. Otherwise one may **actually add and charge** s0 I with s0>=max(0,h-a); then H_aut+s0 I>=0. It changes the phase by exp(-is0t), the mean and scalar by s0, and the full norm budget. This optional model is distinguished throughout.

The new occupation N_X commutes with H_aut even though N_C may change. On N_X=1,

    K_X=I/a_c+D_a,  D_a=i(T_M-T_M*)/(2a_c),
    |k'>=M^-1/2 sum_j exp(2pi i k'j/M)|j>,
    D_a|k'>=sin(omega k'a_c)|k'>/a_c.

Supply the independent coherent state

    chi_k=(2k+1)^-1/2 sum_(k'=-k)^k |k'>,
    phi_a(t)=exp(-itK_X)chi_k.                            (15)

The sign of the hopping and this Fourier convention are paired. The actual free-clock phase1/a_c is retained. There is no projection, readout or postselection on X during evolution.

For a requested clock prepared-isometry error0<b<=1, set Z=B_var S_c/b, choose certified integers

    R_f=k>=max(1,2Z^2),
    n_D>=max(2,6cT,log_2(32/b)),
    r_D=n_D-1,   B_mom=k+R_f r_D,
    M>=2B_mom+R_f+1,
    M^2>=[2T S_c^2 omega^3/(3b)](B_mom^3+k^3),            (16)

and round M upwards to a multiple of four. The accepted c7a theorem applies to arbitrary finite H0, with no commutation hypothesis and no need for data support restrictions in its analytic estimate. It gives, uniformly0<=t<=T,

    ||exp(-itH_aut)(chi_k tensor I)-phi_a(t) tensor U0(t)||
       <= d_R+d_k+4E_(r_D)(T)+T(delta_(B_mom)+delta_k)<=b,
    d_R=B_var S_c/sqrt[8(R_f+1)],
    d_k=B_var S_c/sqrt[8(2k+1)],
    E_r(T)=sum_(j>=r+1)(cT)^j/j!,
    delta_m=a_c^2(omega m)^3/6.                           (17)

The strict guard in(16) is necessary for ordinary Fourier compression. Its proof has two different Dyson-tail comparisons: continuum-to-band and ring-to-band. Sine dispersion and comparison with the **actual** free clock are both paid. The bound does not assume the actual interacting clock follows its free distribution, replace ordinary compression by a cyclic shift, or drop scalar phases. We reuse that complete accepted argument rather than claim a new generic clock theorem. Adding s0 I multiplies the operator target in(17) by exp(-is0t) and leaves its bound unchanged.

## 5. Conditional autonomous full-output result and window

Apply(17) to the complete data DCEA and its passive references R,S, then purify. This costs at most2b in retained X-data-reference trace norm. Combining with(10), for every actual t=t0+s with0<=s<=w,

    ||rho_aut(t)-|phi_a(t)><phi_a(t)| tensor Omega_aged(s)||_1
       <=epsilon_aged=min(2,2b+delta_r+2B t_s).            (18)

The analogous free-old target(11) costs

    epsilon_free=min(2,2b+delta_r+2B(t_c+t_s)).            (19)

No factor is omitted: X remains as the freely evolving comparison clock, C is approximately vacuum, the full previous C information is in E with its old/reference correlations, and F/S retain compression trash and its purifier. The clock is only approximately decoupled. There is no assertion of exact return, catalysis, entropy loss or a reusable reservoir.

For any finite positive error allocations, choose r by rational iteration from q_bar until q_r<=delta^2/(4n); choose t_s<=epsilon_s/(2B) using a certified upper B, choose t_c<=epsilon_c/(2B) only if(19) is desired, and b<=epsilon_X/2. Equations(16) are then finite sufficient clock choices for the complete chosen T=t_c+t_s+w. No equality oracle for a computable real ceiling is needed: larger certified integers suffice. The time does not include a hidden recurrence, but it does include every compression and reset slot and the whole specified window. Pure-clock preparation or storage before t=0 is separately accounted for in section8.

In the aged contract t_c may be long, but its real H0 aging is retained. In either contract a fixed insufficient local strength cap can obstruct the given sufficient recipe: even the comparator needs c, and(16) makes clock and program strengths grow. The theorem is not a common-cap, optimality or efficient-autonomy statement.

The window is a uniform unperturbed state statement at actual time. It is not an automatic stop or a physical detector. V_X is static and generally nonzero even when the comparator waveform has ended. The bound says this continuing interaction has sufficiently small prepared-map effect through T; it does not switch off V_X. Increasing w requires a new finite choice of clock parameters. A later recurrence of the clock/program is not a fresh run of a restored memory.

An optional entry extension is precise but different. Append one positive onsite logarithm F_e=(pi/2)(I-X_(v0)) over a slot t_p>0 before the zero interval. Replace p by p+1, A by A+pi, I_ctl by I_ctl+pi/2, c by max(c,pi/t_p), and T by t_c+t_s+t_p+w. The finite-reservoir entry residual adds2G_e t_p, with G_e=sqrt(alpha0^2+2Lambda|z0|^2). At s=0 the target is entry_C tensor exp[-i(t_s+t_p)K]T_CE sigma^c T_CE* tensor omega_FS. At later s its target is its **full exp(-isH0) conjugation**, with E/F/R/S retained. It is not a stationary ready head or free-K-only evolution. The accepted boundary-word theorem may separately replace that later evolution by its moving-clock/word comparator on its specified interval, adding its full error and preserving the order exp(-isK)W exp[-i(t_c+t_s+t_p)K] in the free-old case. No such word error or physical reader is silently included in(18).

## 6. Physical support, incidence and the exact scalar

The inherited memory rays a_(u,j)=e(u)+j d_u,0<=j<Q are disjoint and avoid the old chain and C. Their coordinates and all reset NN pairs are copied in the complete biased source, section5. They occupy the box

    [-Q-1,x_max] x [1-L_b,2] x [-1,1],
    x_max=max(n_old-1,Q).

No arbitrary extra occupied old sites are assumed here. Additional sites require a newly checked vacancy/box condition. Place the M clock qubits on the square perimeter with corners

    (x_max+2,1-L_b,3), (x_max+2+q_c,1-L_b,3),
    (x_max+2+q_c,1-L_b+q_c,3), (x_max+2,1-L_b+q_c,3),
    q_c=M/4.                                             (20)

Take each corner once. The M clock-clock bonds, including closure, are ordinary NN; these new sites avoid the data box. The added physical qubit count including original C is n(1+Q)+M. The original C/ray/reset selected NN edges number L_b+14+nQ; add M clock NN bonds. These edge counts do **not** count the program terms as NN interactions.

Each program piece n_j tensor V_(R,E)(x_j) acts on one clock qubit and a single data pair, hence at most three qubits. Its ordinary Manhattan diameter is at most

    x_max+Q+7+q_c+max(L_b+1,q_c).                         (21)

The displayed whole construction fits in an integer box of at most
5[x_max+Q+4+q_c] max(L_b+2,q_c+1) sites. Unused positions in that box are not implicitly prepared resources or assumed free of drift; only declared occupied sites and supplied isolation enter the construction. There are at most M u program blocks, where u is the number of distinct addressed data supports, u<=nQ for reset-only. The entry extension adds one onsite support. Stating the finite geometry does not fabricate the nonlocal three-body program terms.

For each data site i, let A_i=sum_(p:i in support F_p)||F_p||, including reset and optional entry. Because R_f<M, exact finite quadrature of(12) yields a_c sum_j F_(R_f)(x_j-t)=1. Applying the triangle inequality **before** this sum gives

    sum_j sum_(E contains i)||V_(R,E)(x_j)||<=A_i/a_c,
    sum_j sum_E||V_(R,E)(x_j)||<=A/a_c.                  (22)

Thus each clock site has whole-term load at most2/a_c+c; a data site has its actual unchanged H0 load plus A_i/a_c. All-sector bounds are

    ||K_X||<=M/a_c,     ||V_X||<=A/a_c<=Mc,
    ||H_aut+s0 I||<=|a|+beta+s0+(M+A)/a_c.               (23)

These full-space costs cannot be replaced by the N_X=1 norms2/a_c and c when pricing leakage or hardware. Assigning a global identity reserve to one site charges s0 to that site's bookkeeping; no homogeneous cap is asserted. The full support/positivity of implemented errors is a separate engineering certificate.

Let k0 be the normalized full trace of H0, i.e. its Pauli identity coefficient; for this boundary k0=k_scalar+B/2. Fourier quadrature also fixes the scalar of the full autonomous operator exactly:

    scalar(H_aut+s0 I)=k0+s0+M/(2a_c)+I_ctl/(2a_c).        (24)

In reset-only I_ctl=A/4, so the last term is A/(8a_c). It differs from the prepared clock mean1/a_c. Dropping a scalar from a data pulse log becomes a clock-position-dependent onsite term in(14), not generally a harmless global phase. Section9 gives an exact three-qubit witness. All original and control scalar costs remain present.

## 7. Initial energy, covariance, conservation and preparation moments

For the exact initial clock(15), define p_j=|chi_k(j)|^2, Vbar=sum_j p_j V_R(x_j), Xi=sum_j p_j V_R(x_j)^2. The clock mean and variance are

    <K_X>=1/a_c,
    v_X=(2k+1)^-1 sum_(l=-k)^k sin^2(2pi l/M)/a_c^2
        <=omega^2 k(k+1)/3.                              (25)

The arbitrary data marginal rho is that of sigma_DCR tensor Theta_AS. The exact initial total moments for H_aut+s0 I are

    mu=1/a_c+s0+Tr rho(H0+Vbar),
    Var=v_X+Tr rho[H0^2+H0 Vbar+Vbar H0+Xi]
                  -[Tr rho(H0+Vbar)]^2
        <=v_X+(beta+c)^2.                                (26)

The last inequality uses H0-aI only as a bound center. Xi is not Vbar squared. The symmetric packet cancels the free-clock/program covariance, as the accepted Fourier proof pairs l with-l-q; the strict alias guard ensures the same finite matrix elements. The product clock state cancels free-clock/H0 covariance. H0–program covariance generally remains, including noncommuting old terms, and appears explicitly in(26). A different or imperfect clock packet need not preserve either cancellation.

The full nominal autonomous Hamiltonian is static, so its total mean and variance are conserved. Its separate pieces need not be. The exact mean balance is

    Delta<K_X>+Delta<H0>+Delta<V_X>=0.                    (27)

No clock-energy loss equals the data gain after discarding the interaction term. The clock need not monotonically lose energy. Trace closeness of a large clock is not an energy-cost refund. The new initial clock coherence, mean1/a_c, variance(25), full norm and program interaction are charged; no external pulse-work integral is asserted to describe this closed autonomous model. Its initial installation and preparation are still supplied physical operations.

For the vacuum target(9), the same installed H0 has mean Tr(K sigma_D^c) and variance Var_(sigma_D^c)(K); for(11), use sigma_D. At a complete trace error epsilon, its mean error is at most beta epsilon, its centered second-moment error at most beta^2 epsilon, and its variance error at most3beta^2 epsilon. Linear reference-valued centered moments of orders1,2 obey beta^j epsilon in trace norm. These are bounded-operator continuity estimates, not conditional variances, energy measurement or physical Record claims. For the entry extension the target mean/variance at s=0 add alpha0 and Q_e respectively, and exact subsequent H0 evolution conserves those nominal moments. Total autonomous-energy comparisons instead require the much larger bound(23), with the appropriate restored scalar for raw moments.

The memory has not been refreshed. Compression preserves its entropy and moves polarization entropy into F/correlations; reset transfers the previous C information into E. The independent program clock adds a supplied pure resource rather than eliminating purity consumption. No thermodynamic advantage over directly supplying fresh pure reset memory is proved.

## 8. State preparation, calibration and actual observation time

The programmed device starts from chi_k independently of the whole data/reference state in(2). It uses M physical clock qubits, not log M, with a coherent one-excitation packet. The accepted clock proof gives an optional at-most-M+1 addressed-gate preparation from a clean vacuum, but that recipe assumes its own timed control and removal/compensation of preparation drift. It is **not** adopted here as an autonomous supplier. If data is present while X is being prepared, H0 aging and any X-data interaction during that entire interval need a new preparation comparison. Either the supplied initial sigma in(2) is the actual state at the declared start, or that prior evolution must be explicitly paid. A pure clock does not appear for free because its static Hamiltonian is positive.

Let the actual complete initial state have trace error eta_init from the stated one, and let the implemented full Hermitian Hamiltonian be H_aut+s0 I+E(t), with references passive and

    eta_H(T)=integral_0^T ||E(t)||dt.

Add eta_init+2eta_H(T) to(18) or(19), capped at2. This includes clock-number leakage, H0 error, clock hopping phase/strength, program coefficients, unwanted memory self-Hamiltonians, reserve and unlisted couplings. A prepared-sector matrix error is not a full-space certificate for leakage. For example, if each of the M clock bonds, at most M u program blocks and a reserve term has full operator error at most xi, plus background error eta0_H, a conservative sufficient norm bound is eta0_H+(M+M u+1)xi; multiply by the whole actual elapsed duration. Tolerances must shrink with these counts and with moment objectives.

On the exact N_X=1 sector, a safe nominal norm is

    B_1=|a|+beta+s0+2/a_c+c.                              (28)

At a fixed nominal target time t*, an actual time error |Delta t| costs at most2B_1|Delta t|, in addition to full-space implementation integration over the **actual** interval and eta_init. This follows by comparing to the nominal prepared evolution first, so it does not assume leaked states obey the sector norm. For a time-indexed target at any actual t in[t0,t0+w],(18) needs no silent identification of different free-K histories. A physical detector operating through a finite interval is an additional interaction, not justified by the unperturbed window alone.

All effective inputs are finite: the complete K/H_app coefficients and certified bounds; q_bar, r and the explicit word; positive rational durations and error lower bounds; actual site/isolation declarations; certified Fourier, pi and coefficient approximations; and full-space precision allowances. Larger certified bounds and integers determine(16). No data-dependent perfect energy measurement, infinite clock or hidden recurrence search is invoked. These finite existence/certificate formulas are not an emitted enormous table or a demonstrated common-cap device.

## 9. The unresolved ordinary-NN two-qubit interface and two failed shortcuts

The current static matrix(14) supplies a finite internal timing system, but is not yet the requested fully local implementation. Already one reset pair exposes the issue. For a clock bit x and data pair c,e, the sampled positive SWAP logarithm contains

    B_x=n_x tensor (I-S_ce)/2
       =[III-ZII-IXX-IYY-IZZ+ZXX+ZYY+ZZZ]/8.              (29)

The physical logarithm is pi B_x. Pauli strings are orthogonal in Hilbert–Schmidt inner product. The three weight-three coefficients1/8 cannot be produced by any sum of operators acting on at most two of these same three factors. The squared Hilbert–Schmidt distance from that linear space is3/8 for B_x (and3pi^2/8 for pi B_x). This proves failure only of an exact same-factor rewriting. It excludes neither ancillary gadgets nor a different approximate autonomous construction.

Dropping the scalar1/4 from the data singlet projector changes B_x to B_x-n_x/4. On |000> it still has eigenvalue0, but on |100> its eigenvalue becomes-1/4. At duration pi in these dimensionless units this introduces relative exp(i pi/4) on the latter vector. Starting x in |+> and data in|00>, the full clock-output trace-distance squared is2-sqrt(2). Thus a gate's data-global phase becomes physically relative in a clock-controlled program. It cannot be erased by a single global scalar adjustment. Restoring the omitted clock onsite term repairs this particular mutation; the construction retains it from the outset.

A second failed shortcut is the usual exact prefix gauge with unchanged arbitrary background. For W=|0><0|_x tensor I+|1><1|_x tensor S_ce,

    W*(I_x tensor n_c)W
       =|0><0|_x tensor n_c+|1><1|_x tensor n_e,           (30)

whose difference from I_x tensor n_c has norm1. In general a program prefix conjugates H0 to different blocks. The arbitrary-H clock estimate(17) retains chronological H0 and pays finite clock error; it never asserts the incorrect background factorization. Equation(30) is a local counterexample, not a ban on other compensated or autonomous designs.

